From: Marek Czernohous <mczernohous@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau: MCP79 EVO SV-rescue (0019) + Tesla channel-kill dead-letter fix (0020a/b)

Rev 2 (post adversarial review). Two independent, source-verified fixes for the aging
NVAC/MCP79, additive on the 0011-0018 soft-dpms stack, each gated by a runtime module
parameter. Review fixes folded in: 0019 armed path now finalises the synthesized SV1
under disp->super.mutex (serialises vs the supervisor worker); a diagnose-armed stage
(sv_rescue=2, probe at trigger, no write) precedes the armed stage (3); 0020a moves the
kill-event unsubscribe before the fence-context teardown (closes a narrow killed-event
UAF window newly reachable on Tesla); mode>1 rejected. 0020b (disp_fence_timeout_ms)
unchanged, review-clean. Combining chan_kill_event=0 disp_fence_timeout_ms=0 sv_rescue=0
restores prior behaviour without a rebuild.
---
